course: dictionary
lesson: 1282
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, so you need the context to know which one is right. The word butt is one of them. «Goats can butt hard enough to knock a child over.» Here butt means to hit something with your head, because goats do that.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. Does "to hit with the head" make sense in «the goat will butt you»? Yes, so that is the right meaning. Now look at «the butt of the joke». Here butt is a noun, and it means the person people laugh at.
explain: Butt can also be part of a phrase. «Please don't butt in while we are talking» means don't interrupt rudely. Phrases like this are often best learned as a whole, not word by word.
explain: Words also change between places. «Butt» means mate, a friend, in South Wales. In the UK, a water butt is a large barrel that catches rainwater from a roof, so you can use it to water plants.
fact: Butt can be a noun or a verb, so it can name a thing or show an action.
fact: «Butt» (verb) means to hit something with your head, like a goat.
fact: «Butt in» means to interrupt someone rudely.
fact: «The butt of the joke» means the person people laugh at.
fact: A water butt is a large barrel that collects rainwater, and «butt» means mate in South Wales.
exercise: «Goats can butt hard enough to knock a child over.» What does butt mean here? | To sing loudly | To sit down on the bottom | To tidy up a room | *To hit something with your head
exercise: In the UK, a water butt collects rain from the roof. What is a water butt? | *A large barrel that holds rainwater | A pipe that carries water to the sea | A kind of garden tool | A small bucket for washing hands
exercise: Ruby says, "Don't butt in while we are talking." What does butt in mean? | To hit a ball with a bat | *To interrupt someone rudely | To help someone carry a box | To hide behind a door
test: «Sam felt like the butt of the joke when everyone laughed at his hat.» What is the butt of the joke? | The place where the party was held | The hat that was lost | *The person people laugh at | The joke that everyone tells
test: In South Wales, what does «butt» mean? | Bottom | Goat | Barrel | *Mate
exam: «Pachycephalosaurus had a bony dome; scientists argue whether it head-butted like goats.» What does head-butted mean here? | Ran away very fast | Sang a loud song | Slept under a rock | *Hit something with its head
